3. Vendored client half — build/session-eva-status.js
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The file started as a byte-for-byte copy of code from another plugin, not written
for this theme (see the caveats at the end of this section). The upstream is MIT and
by the same author as this theme:

  build/session-eva-status.js
    Upstream: dsh-session-eva-status v0.1.0
    Source:   https://github.com/WhatCannotBeSaid/dsh-session-eva-status
    License:  MIT

MIT requires its copyright notice and license text to travel with copies and
substantial portions. The upstream repository carries them in its own LICENSE
file; the full MIT text and the copyright line are section 1 of this
repository's LICENSE. The file carries no notice of its own, and it is inlined into
the generated client.js, so if you redistribute the file or the bundle, carry this
section with it.

One caveat, added 2026-10-09.
build/session-eva-status.js (D78) is no longer a byte-for-byte copy: this repository
patches spots in its hot path — a frame-coalesced schedule, a
compare-then-write pin attribute, and cancelling the pending frame on dispose —
because the upstream checkout is not available here to fix and re-vendor.
The list is at the top of the file; the original contract tripwires remain in
cli.23, cli.24 and cli.27 of tools/selfcheck.mjs. Current patch inventory is
maintained in the file header and docs/optimization-s1-s10.md: status rail a-f
(including scoped lookup, compositor breathing and fallback mutation wakeups). New
behavior is covered by tools/runtime.test.mjs. No pristine upstream checkout/hash
was available for this change; this does not claim byte equivalence to upstream.
Refreshing the file from upstream must re-apply and test the listed patches.

Removed 2026-10-25 (eva-inspired-theme 1.3.0): build/plugin-toggle.js was dropped
from this repository. dsh-disable-unofficial-plugins is published on its own now,
so the theme no longer vendors, patches or ships any part of it; install it
separately to get the switch.

D82's host-bundle exclusion went with it: that protection only existed because the
vendored copy sat inside the theme's own client bundle, so it is now the standalone
plugin's business, not the theme's.


4. Background wallpapers — NOT redistributed, linked by URL
-----------------------------------------------------------

This repository carries no image bytes for a background. `build/wallpapers.json`
(tracked) names two third-party pictures by URL; the build turns those into CSS
`url()` values, and the browser fetches each one from the host its entry names
(haowallpaper.com for the light default, wallhaven for the dark one) when the
theme paints. Nothing here is a copy of either picture, and this project licenses
nothing in them.

  og33jl — https://wallhaven.cc/w/og33jl
    Artist:            YOTA SAKI (credited on that page)
    Original posting:  https://www.pixiv.net/en/artworks/133258822
    Uploaded there by: Elisban
    2560x1440. Dark-mode default.

  eva01city — https://haowallpaper.com/homeViewLook/18703364605463936
    Artist:            unknown — the page credits only its uploader
    Also on wallhaven: https://wallhaven.cc/w/x85po3 (uploaded there by BachoWilson)
    1100x775. Light-mode default. Anonymous visitors are served only this preview;
    the artwork's own file is 3066x2160.

Neither artist has licensed this use, and neither has been asked. If you are one
of them and object to the link, ask and the entry will be dropped from the
manifest; this repository holds no copy of either picture either way.

